  "problem": "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $g:[0,2]\\to {0,2}?$\n\n- The domain of $g$ is ${0,2}$\n- The codomain of $g$ is ${0,2}$\n- The range of $g$ is $[0,2]$",
  "worked_solution": "The notation \n\n$$\ng:[0,2]\\to {0,2}\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $g$ maps the set $[0,2]$ to the set ${0,2}.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $[0,2],$ and\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is ${0,2}.$ Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
